B-Minor grammar (EBNF)

program        = { declaration } EOF ;
declaration    = identifier ":" ( function_decl | variable_decl ) ;
variable_decl  = type [ "=" initializer ] ";" ;
function_decl  = "function" return_type "(" [ parameters ] ")" ( ";" | "=" block ) ;
parameters     = parameter { "," parameter } ;
parameter      = identifier ":" type ;
return_type    = atomic_type | "void" ;
type           = atomic_type | "array" "[" [ expression ] "]" type ;
atomic_type    = "integer" | "boolean" | "char" | "string" ;
initializer    = expression ;

block          = "{" { declaration | statement } "}" ;
statement      = block
               | "return" [ expression ] ";"
               | "print" [ expression { "," expression } ] ";"
               | "if" "(" expression ")" statement [ "else" statement ]
               | "for" "(" [ expression ] ";" [ expression ] ";" [ expression ] ")" statement
               | [ expression ] ";" ;

expression     = assignment ;
assignment     = logic_or [ "=" assignment ] ;
logic_or       = logic_and { "||" logic_and } ;
logic_and      = equality { "&&" equality } ;
equality       = comparison { ( "==" | "!=" ) comparison } ;
comparison     = addition { ( "<" | "<=" | ">" | ">=" ) addition } ;
addition       = multiplication { ( "+" | "-" ) multiplication } ;
multiplication = power { ( "*" | "/" | "%" ) power } ;
power          = unary [ "^" power ] ;
unary          = ( "!" | "-" ) unary | postfix ;
postfix        = primary { "(" [ arguments ] ")" | "[" expression "]" | "++" | "--" } ;
arguments      = expression { "," expression } ;
primary        = identifier | integer_literal | boolean_literal | char_literal
               | string_literal | "(" expression ")" | array_initializer ;
array_initializer = "{" [ expression { "," expression } [ "," ] ] "}" ;

boolean_literal = "true" | "false" ;

Token descriptions

letter         = [A-Za-z]
digit          = [0-9]
identifier     = [A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*
integer       = [0-9]+
string         = \"(\\.|[^\"\\\r\n])*\"
character      = '(\\.|[^'\\\r\n])'
line_comment   = //[non-newline]*
block_comment  = /\\* ... first occurrence of *\\/
space          = [ \\t\\r\\n]+
operators      = == != <= >= && || ++ -- + - * / % ^ = ! < >
delimiters     = ( ) [ ] { } ; , :
keywords       = array boolean char else false for function if integer print return string true void while

The longest token is consumed first. A keyword has priority over an identifier
of the same length. Whitespace and comments do not enter the parser. Each
non-ignored token has its original spelling, file, line and column.

Parsing approach: recursive descent, with loops instead of left recursion.
Expressions use precedence levels and right-associative assignment and exponentiation.
An AST node stores its kind, starting location and a type field left empty for
later semantic analysis. Unrecognized characters become INVALID tokens.
The parser skips unexpected tokens to ;, }, if, for, print or return.

(* Grammar Notes
   This file defines the syntax of the B-Minor language.
   The parser implementation is located in main.cpp.
   Lexical analysis recognizes tokens before parsing.
*)